WEBVTT

01:49.192 --> 01:56.199
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:59.452 --> 02:01.955
We have conducted
extensive research and experimentation

02:02.747 --> 02:05.250
on the limitations of the human body.

02:23.560 --> 02:27.981
We discovered the existence of the Najin
during one of those experiments.

03:20.658 --> 03:23.953
So, it was all a coincidence?

03:25.246 --> 03:29.292
It's like the Penicillium
that appeared in a petri dish.

03:29.375 --> 03:34.339
Much like how that chance discovery
of mold changed the course

03:34.422 --> 03:36.466
of the history of human diseases…

03:38.509 --> 03:43.848
the discovery of the Najin will lead
humanity to the next level of evolution.

03:43.932 --> 03:45.808
Are you referring to the healing ability?

03:47.018 --> 03:47.852
Perhaps.

03:49.520 --> 03:52.065
But we believe
it holds potential for more.

03:53.650 --> 03:54.734
I see.

03:56.069 --> 03:58.154
Thank you for the explanation.

04:01.950 --> 04:07.288
Director Ichiro
will be returning to Japan soon.

04:09.958 --> 04:13.127
You can take his place
in charge of Ongseong Hospital

04:13.878 --> 04:16.714
and complete your ongoing experiments.

04:17.715 --> 04:21.678
I will support you
by whatever means necessary.

04:25.765 --> 04:30.270
I cannot guarantee how long it will take
or how much money will be needed.

04:31.437 --> 04:33.231
Nothing is certain as of now.

04:33.314 --> 04:34.899
That doesn't matter.

04:35.858 --> 04:39.362
Seishin is what I want, after all.

04:40.530 --> 04:43.449
Your job is to make her
obey me completely.

04:44.826 --> 04:46.411
That's all you need to do.

05:41.174 --> 05:42.425
Mr. Ishikawa.

05:47.722 --> 05:50.600
So, it was you all along?

05:56.272 --> 05:58.441
Have you been
wandering around in that state

05:59.233 --> 06:01.652
killing people for the past three days?

06:02.737 --> 06:04.072
Mr. Ishikawa.

06:07.367 --> 06:10.995
What in the world happened to you, Akiko?

06:13.247 --> 06:14.999
Help me, Mr. Ishikawa.

06:26.094 --> 06:27.512
Go back to Ongseong Hospital.

06:29.764 --> 06:32.266
You have murdered more than ten people.

06:32.809 --> 06:36.145
You will be executed anyway, Akiko.

06:43.486 --> 06:44.695
What about the baby?

06:46.155 --> 06:47.323
Our baby--

06:47.407 --> 06:48.449
Look at yourself!

06:50.618 --> 06:53.663
How can you still expect me
to acknowledge that baby as my own?

06:56.541 --> 06:59.252
Don't make things
any more difficult for me, Akiko.

07:09.345 --> 07:10.555
Get in there yourself.

07:12.432 --> 07:16.102
This is the last act of kindness
I can offer you.

07:19.647 --> 07:21.566
Stop stalling and get in.

07:25.319 --> 07:26.320
Now!

07:35.079 --> 07:36.205
What are you doing?

08:36.349 --> 08:37.600
Commissioner!

08:37.683 --> 08:39.018
Commissioner Ishikawa!

08:40.311 --> 08:41.604
Get him to the car!

08:42.730 --> 08:45.399
Commissioner! Stay with me!

09:01.082 --> 09:04.418
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN PREDATOR AND PREY

09:04.502 --> 09:07.088
EPISODE 9
ATROCITY

09:33.239 --> 09:34.156
Father.

09:45.126 --> 09:46.294
I'm coming in.

10:19.410 --> 10:20.494
Chae-ok.

10:21.704 --> 10:24.457
I'm heading over to where your mother is.

10:26.751 --> 10:28.502
Hey! Who goes there?

10:29.003 --> 10:30.004
Stop!

10:31.297 --> 10:32.882
Stop or we'll shoot!

10:37.511 --> 10:39.347
I am here to find my wife.

10:41.641 --> 10:43.934
Go and tell the person named Kato

10:45.978 --> 10:49.565
that the Seishin you are experimenting on
in the underground laboratory

10:51.400 --> 10:52.443
is my wife.

10:54.570 --> 10:59.116
I am going to fulfill
my last duty as her husband.

11:00.451 --> 11:01.869
So, Chae-ok,

11:03.245 --> 11:05.289
go on with your life.

11:06.832 --> 11:07.667
Please

11:08.584 --> 11:11.003
cherish your life dearly.

11:35.361 --> 11:37.780
Colonel Kato, we brought the man.

11:54.463 --> 11:56.674
You're Seishin's husband?

11:57.717 --> 11:58.759
I am.

12:01.721 --> 12:03.514
Let me meet my wife.

12:42.803 --> 12:44.513
It's been ten years, correct?

12:47.433 --> 12:48.434
How does it feel

12:49.393 --> 12:50.895
to see your wife again

12:52.730 --> 12:54.732
for the first time in ten years?

12:55.524 --> 12:57.359
You evil bastards.

12:59.779 --> 13:00.613
How…

13:02.448 --> 13:03.449
How could you…

13:05.326 --> 13:07.453
You sons of bitches!

13:08.162 --> 13:09.497
Fucking bastards!

13:09.580 --> 13:11.081
Let go of me! Let go!

13:11.874 --> 13:13.209
Sons of bitches!

13:14.418 --> 13:17.463
You bastards,
how could you do something like this?

13:17.546 --> 13:19.048
How could you?!

14:01.799 --> 14:03.551
We managed to calm it with food,

14:04.134 --> 14:07.096
but what should we do now?
It's becoming violent again, sir.

14:08.931 --> 14:09.932
I guess

14:11.141 --> 14:16.313
there really is no other way
than to find its child.

14:34.248 --> 14:35.416
What do we do?

14:35.916 --> 14:38.002
We can't turn a blind eye.

14:38.794 --> 14:42.965
Yet even if we were to help her,
there's not much we can do.

14:51.891 --> 14:53.475
We'll have to think of a way.

14:54.184 --> 14:56.520
You can't go back to Ongseong Hospital.

14:57.146 --> 14:59.315
Don't even think about it, okay?

15:05.571 --> 15:06.739
Look here!

15:07.281 --> 15:10.075
Why in the world
would you do such evil things?

15:10.159 --> 15:14.121
A hospital is where you treat people,
not do such damned things!

15:15.331 --> 15:16.332
Well,

15:17.416 --> 15:21.921
I'm not really aware
of what goes on in there.

15:22.004 --> 15:25.090
Now you know!
So try coming up with a plan!

15:25.174 --> 15:27.676
As a so-called officer
of the police bureau,

15:27.760 --> 15:30.971
you just discovered an illegal act!
Are you just going to sit there?

15:32.014 --> 15:36.268
I just follow orders,
so even if I were to do something,

15:36.852 --> 15:39.688
I wouldn't have any powers.

15:40.606 --> 15:41.607
So you're powerless!

15:41.690 --> 15:45.235
Does that give you an excuse
to go along with every wrong thing?

15:45.319 --> 15:46.403
Excuse me--

15:46.487 --> 15:48.781
You people might run things around here,

15:48.864 --> 15:51.992
but there are things you should
and shouldn't do as human beings!

15:52.076 --> 15:55.329
If you don't know where to draw the line,
can you call yourself human?

15:55.412 --> 15:58.666
How are you any different from an animal?

16:00.793 --> 16:02.127
You're right.

16:04.380 --> 16:08.467
Let's keep the shop closed
until this situation is resolved.

16:10.219 --> 16:13.722
It would also be safer
if we moved Mr. Gu somewhere else.

16:14.556 --> 16:15.641
What is your plan?

16:15.724 --> 16:20.521
When a problem arises,
you must nip it in the bud.

16:21.772 --> 16:22.815
Master!

16:22.898 --> 16:26.735
I saw exactly what's going on
in Ongseong Hospital.

16:28.362 --> 16:33.367
What's happening in there is something
that shouldn't happen to any human being.

16:35.536 --> 16:38.288
But I bet they will deny it
in front of the world

16:39.289 --> 16:44.128
and say that they did no such thing,
that such things never even existed.

16:47.172 --> 16:49.967
Myeong-ja killed so many people, but look,

16:51.010 --> 16:53.012
not one paper covered the murders.

16:55.055 --> 16:56.473
This is how they operate.

16:57.182 --> 17:00.394
They cover things up
as if they never happened at all.

17:00.477 --> 17:01.437
But sir--

17:01.520 --> 17:04.064
As you said,
there are clear rights and wrongs.

17:05.816 --> 17:09.194
If we turn a blind eye
because it doesn't seem to concern us now,

17:09.820 --> 17:14.074
then the same thing
will eventually happen to all of us.

17:19.121 --> 17:20.122
Tell us.

17:22.207 --> 17:24.209
What can we do to help?

17:28.255 --> 17:32.217
I'm afraid there isn't much
that we can do.

17:32.301 --> 17:35.679
The wounds on his face
and carotid arteries are too wide and deep

17:35.763 --> 17:38.015
for us to stop the bleeding.

17:38.974 --> 17:41.685
- We will do our best.
- Stop the bleeding!

17:41.769 --> 17:44.813
- But if the bleeding continues…
- More gauze! Now!

17:46.065 --> 17:48.108
I'm terribly sorry to say this,

17:49.151 --> 17:51.820
but he may not survive the night,
Lady Maeda.

17:53.030 --> 17:56.450
Oh, well, that is unfortunate.

17:57.367 --> 17:58.285
Pardon?

17:58.368 --> 17:59.953
Anyways,

18:00.662 --> 18:03.290
take good care of my husband, please.

18:03.373 --> 18:04.333
Good night.

18:24.019 --> 18:25.062
Found it.

18:40.702 --> 18:43.247
Lady Maeda, a message from Mr. Shiro.

19:33.130 --> 19:34.214
What were you doing?

19:35.507 --> 19:36.508
You know,

19:37.593 --> 19:38.677
just watching.

19:55.319 --> 19:58.447
The world seems so peaceful
from up here, doesn't it?

19:59.531 --> 20:00.699
There's no pain,

20:02.034 --> 20:03.035
no death…

20:05.662 --> 20:07.372
and no unjustness.

20:08.290 --> 20:09.917
It's all so quiet.

20:15.714 --> 20:18.300
It's hard to see through the darkness now,

20:19.551 --> 20:21.136
but I'm sure that everyone

20:22.804 --> 20:25.557
is holding their breath,
waiting for the night to pass.

20:30.729 --> 20:31.939
What about Myeong-ja?

20:32.814 --> 20:34.066
What happened to her?

20:34.733 --> 20:37.444
It seems she was taken back
to Ongseong Hospital.

20:38.070 --> 20:41.782
And Ishikawa seems to have been
seriously injured in the ordeal.

20:50.958 --> 20:53.919
So Father and Myeong-ja
are both back in that hospital.

20:59.591 --> 21:00.759
Could it be that…

21:04.471 --> 21:07.307
we'll never be able to stop
what they are doing?

21:16.942 --> 21:18.944
Will you come with me?

21:19.444 --> 21:20.946
I have something to show you.

21:41.133 --> 21:42.551
What is all this?

21:42.634 --> 21:44.303
This is my collection.

21:46.054 --> 21:48.515
Some things were pawned
and never reclaimed,

21:49.141 --> 21:51.476
and others I bought from time to time.

21:51.560 --> 21:53.478
That's the nature of a pawnshop.

21:54.146 --> 21:56.982
Every item that comes in
has its own story.

22:00.319 --> 22:01.236
Yes.

22:02.154 --> 22:05.991
That gramophone belonged to Wang Su-bok,
the courtesan from Pyeongyang.

22:08.744 --> 22:09.661
And…

22:10.579 --> 22:13.081
that coat hanging over there,

22:13.165 --> 22:16.918
Mr. Yun Dong-ju pawned it so he could buy
his fellow students some food,

22:17.794 --> 22:20.714
but he didn't make it back to reclaim it.

22:22.257 --> 22:25.010
And this is Na Hye-seok's work.

22:26.428 --> 22:29.931
She is a genius who had her work
shown at the Joseon Art Exhibition.

22:30.932 --> 22:34.519
I suppose living as an artist
is not all smooth sailing.

22:34.603 --> 22:38.231
Mrs. Nawol chided me for paying too much
for a painting of little value,

22:39.024 --> 22:40.692
but I like her drawings.

22:43.570 --> 22:45.697
I have a few more of her pieces, actually.

22:54.498 --> 22:55.665
Could you

22:57.542 --> 22:58.794
give me your hand?

23:20.482 --> 23:24.361
I bought this silver bracelet
from an American missionary.

23:25.779 --> 23:28.365
Embedded in the middle
is a thing called an opal.

23:29.324 --> 23:32.661
I heard it is considered
a lucky stone in Europe.

23:35.997 --> 23:36.832
There.

23:38.375 --> 23:41.711
You will only experience good luck
from now on.

23:53.432 --> 23:55.767
I have many more interesting items.

23:56.268 --> 23:59.438
We can look through them later,
whenever we have time.

23:59.521 --> 24:00.439
Let's

24:01.690 --> 24:03.442
make a promise to each other.

24:09.364 --> 24:12.534
If either of us ends up dying
before the other…

24:15.829 --> 24:18.165
whoever remains has to remember…

24:20.709 --> 24:22.127
the other person.

24:24.379 --> 24:25.380
What do you think?

24:34.306 --> 24:36.475
I don't feel that sad about dying…

24:41.605 --> 24:45.275
but if no one in this world remembers
even a trace of my existence…

24:50.322 --> 24:51.781
that would make me feel…

24:54.242 --> 24:55.660
a little lonesome.

25:02.834 --> 25:06.254
I'm sorry, but it won't come to that.

25:09.799 --> 25:11.134
Because the two of us

25:12.844 --> 25:15.931
will be together,
even through the good times.

25:22.395 --> 25:23.688
Do you really think…

25:28.276 --> 25:30.278
those good times will come to us?

25:35.700 --> 25:36.618
They will.

25:38.870 --> 25:40.080
I will make sure…

25:42.624 --> 25:44.376
that they come to us.

25:46.503 --> 25:47.420
So--

26:06.356 --> 26:07.274
Stay with me.

26:10.110 --> 26:11.278
Stay…

26:13.822 --> 26:14.906
right by my side.

28:18.446 --> 28:19.656
Be safe.

28:20.365 --> 28:21.700
Take care of yourself.

28:43.972 --> 28:45.807
Keep watch over the shop.

28:46.433 --> 28:47.892
Don't forget to lock the doors.

28:48.852 --> 28:50.603
I will. Goodbye.

29:40.695 --> 29:41.529
Tae-sang!

29:47.202 --> 29:48.036
You're safe.

29:49.162 --> 29:50.413
Thank goodness.

29:50.497 --> 29:51.748
What a relief.

30:58.606 --> 31:00.358
My sincere condolences.

31:06.155 --> 31:08.408
I'm afraid I have no choice, Mr. Ishikawa.

31:08.992 --> 31:11.578
I must do this to keep my position here.

31:11.661 --> 31:15.498
Please direct your resentment
toward Lady Maeda.

31:16.457 --> 31:18.459
This is all according to her will.

31:19.377 --> 31:20.211
No…

31:21.796 --> 31:22.964
No…

31:27.385 --> 31:28.887
Help me…

31:48.948 --> 31:53.912
I would like my husband's death
to be more honorable.

31:55.663 --> 31:57.874
A commissioner of the Government-General

31:58.541 --> 32:01.210
murdered by a Joseon-born courtesan.

32:01.294 --> 32:05.256
Imagine how shameful that would be
for the police bureau as well.

32:06.174 --> 32:07.008
Yes, ma'am.

32:11.971 --> 32:14.682
COMMISSIONER ISHIKAWA DIES
WHILE ARRESTING JOSEON-BORN SERIAL KILLER

32:14.766 --> 32:17.018
Ishikawa died early this morning.

32:18.019 --> 32:20.855
A Joseon person
becomes the offender once again.

32:22.607 --> 32:24.567
It's always the same pattern, isn't it?

32:25.360 --> 32:29.030
They hide, fabricate, and distort
the facts to cover up their wrongdoings.

32:30.365 --> 32:34.702
And if that doesn't work, they will turn
their swords to the Joseon people again.

32:35.578 --> 32:37.080
Think about the Kantō earthquake.

32:37.163 --> 32:39.749
What would they have done without us?

32:40.416 --> 32:42.585
They blame us whenever something happens.

32:44.128 --> 32:46.589
They will choose
one of two methods, as always.

32:47.131 --> 32:49.384
Either take it out
on the innocent citizens…

32:49.467 --> 32:52.428
Or take it out on us.

32:54.931 --> 32:57.892
Why us? What crime have we committed?

32:57.976 --> 33:00.186
The crime of knowing too much, I suppose.

33:00.687 --> 33:05.400
About the underground lab in the hospital,
what occurred there, and even Myeong-ja.

33:07.694 --> 33:10.947
So, what's your plan?

33:14.117 --> 33:15.118
Tell me.

33:16.160 --> 33:20.248
I know you called me here at this hour
because you have a plan in mind.

33:25.128 --> 33:27.088
I now have someone I'd like to protect.

33:28.589 --> 33:29.590
That's why…

33:31.759 --> 33:36.597
I'm thinking of putting my neck
on the line as well.

33:41.477 --> 33:43.813
Do you know what I really fear?

33:47.817 --> 33:49.610
Having a dream

33:51.112 --> 33:53.114
in this hopeless world.

33:56.034 --> 33:58.745
Director Ichiro, have a safe trip back.

34:08.671 --> 34:09.797
Comrade Kwon.

34:27.857 --> 34:32.028
I fear that my resolve will grow weak
because of that vain hope,

34:33.237 --> 34:36.074
that I might hesitate and falter
to do what must be done.

34:38.201 --> 34:39.911
That is what I fear.

34:42.497 --> 34:44.499
And so I bid you goodbye.

34:53.424 --> 34:54.509
Thank you.

34:56.427 --> 34:58.012
Thank you, Master Jang.

35:01.641 --> 35:03.476
I'll always remember you.

35:04.143 --> 35:05.478
Wait, hold on!

35:06.521 --> 35:07.772
So long.

35:09.023 --> 35:10.024
Stop!

35:14.362 --> 35:15.488
You know what?

35:16.614 --> 35:19.367
What I fear the most

35:20.868 --> 35:24.372
is losing those I do not wish to lose.

35:26.791 --> 35:28.334
Director Ichiro has been shot!

35:28.417 --> 35:30.169
Get her!

37:13.272 --> 37:14.482
What did you just say?

37:15.441 --> 37:17.526
With the dynamite you have,

37:17.610 --> 37:20.071
how many bombs can you make?

37:20.154 --> 37:21.697
Why do you ask?

37:22.365 --> 37:24.200
Do you wish to join the rebellion?

37:24.784 --> 37:27.745
Unfortunately, the Bumingwan event
won't be happening.

37:29.622 --> 37:30.456
What?

37:30.539 --> 37:34.377
It appears Ishikawa's funeral ceremony
will be hosted by the Government-General.

37:34.877 --> 37:37.380
The Bumingwan event
has been delayed indefinitely.

37:38.297 --> 37:39.548
Is this confirmed?

37:39.632 --> 37:42.301
We've heard nothing of this
from our sources yet.

37:42.385 --> 37:45.012
This intel came from within,
so I'm sure of it.

37:45.554 --> 37:48.808
I will vouch for its accuracy
and trustworthiness.

37:49.976 --> 37:52.979
In any case,
why did you ask about the bombs?

37:53.062 --> 37:54.647
The rebellion is all but lost now.

37:54.730 --> 37:58.276
I was hoping to use those bombs first.

37:58.943 --> 38:02.405
So you're not here to give us a hand,
but to take the bombs for yourself.

38:02.488 --> 38:05.324
Forget it. I've heard quite enough.

38:06.200 --> 38:07.243
Please leave.

38:08.744 --> 38:11.122
How do you plan on using the bombs?

38:11.205 --> 38:13.249
- Comrade Lee.
- Ongseong Hospital.

38:17.378 --> 38:18.462
My plan…

38:21.132 --> 38:22.717
is to wipe it off the map.

38:29.515 --> 38:30.516
Colonel Kato!

38:31.726 --> 38:32.643
Sir!

38:57.209 --> 38:58.794
We have a problem, Master Jang.

39:00.296 --> 39:02.298
It's about that sleuth, Yoon Chae-ok.

39:03.841 --> 39:05.468
She's caused some trouble.

40:04.777 --> 40:06.779
What happened? Where is the specimen?

40:06.862 --> 40:08.030
We can't see it.

40:08.114 --> 40:12.118
We've been watching for almost an hour,
but there has been no movement.

40:25.798 --> 40:26.882
And the elevator?

40:26.966 --> 40:28.092
It's been shut down.

40:28.759 --> 40:31.011
It's the only way
to get to the upper floors,

40:31.095 --> 40:33.973
which means the specimen
should still be down there.

40:40.312 --> 40:41.647
What do you mean by that?

40:41.730 --> 40:43.482
Chae-ok has disappeared? Where to?

40:44.942 --> 40:46.110
We don't know either.

40:46.777 --> 40:49.780
After that woman shot Director Ichiro,

40:50.281 --> 40:52.700
the officers nearby
chased after her immediately,

40:53.659 --> 40:54.827
but then she vanished.

40:55.411 --> 40:57.872
Officers from Jongno Station
and the police bureau

40:57.955 --> 41:00.583
are searching for her
from Bonjeong to Jongno,

41:01.167 --> 41:03.043
but she's nowhere to be found.

41:05.421 --> 41:08.299
They have just ordered
a search of your shop as well.

41:10.676 --> 41:11.927
- Find her!
- Yes, sir!

41:12.011 --> 41:13.596
Hurry! Search the place!

41:13.679 --> 41:14.847
Yes, sir!

41:17.391 --> 41:18.601
What are you doing?

41:35.242 --> 41:36.327
The situation is

41:37.203 --> 41:39.163
turning from bad to worse.

41:39.997 --> 41:42.124
This could be the last time I can give you

41:44.001 --> 41:45.920
information like this, Mr. Jang.

41:49.507 --> 41:50.508
Thank you.

41:51.008 --> 41:53.427
What you just told me was very helpful.

41:54.011 --> 41:54.845
You should go.

41:57.223 --> 41:59.808
It'd be best to keep your distance
from me for a while.

42:00.309 --> 42:01.310
Do you understand?

42:09.485 --> 42:11.070
Be careful, Mr. Jang!

42:11.153 --> 42:12.738
There is an invisible hand

42:14.532 --> 42:15.866
that controls everything.

42:26.126 --> 42:28.587
How could you let this happen
as the police chief?

42:29.088 --> 42:33.133
A shooting in broad daylight
in front of Lady Maeda's house

42:33.217 --> 42:34.468
while she's in mourning?

42:34.552 --> 42:38.639
My sincerest apologies!
We should have been more vigilant.

42:38.722 --> 42:42.393
This is not only
an act of provocation toward us all,

42:42.476 --> 42:44.186
but a clear act of terrorism.

42:45.145 --> 42:48.899
You must find out who's behind it at once!

42:49.733 --> 42:54.947
Take this opportunity to wipe out
all seditious Joseon-borns in Gyeongseong.

42:55.823 --> 42:58.617
Anyone who is a nuisance
should be dealt with!

42:58.701 --> 43:00.077
- That's right!
- Yes!

43:00.160 --> 43:02.580
- We can't let this go on.
- Let's dispose of them!

43:06.500 --> 43:07.334
Hello?

43:08.502 --> 43:09.461
Shiro?

43:14.383 --> 43:15.551
What is going on?

43:17.011 --> 43:20.264
You promised you would leave
the House of Golden Treasure alone!

43:21.432 --> 43:24.602
You said I just needed to tell you
where the sleuth woman was.

43:24.685 --> 43:28.105
But officers just came
and turned this place upside down!

43:28.772 --> 43:31.442
No, I can't do this anymore.

43:32.192 --> 43:35.321
I quit. Just give me my money.

43:37.364 --> 43:41.035
You promised to put me
on a ship bound for Tokyo.

43:41.619 --> 43:43.454
This is not the time.

43:43.537 --> 43:44.788
We'll talk later.

43:46.165 --> 43:48.334
Hello?

44:03.682 --> 44:04.516
Mr. Gu…

44:10.064 --> 44:11.649
Is it still not moving?

44:13.150 --> 44:13.984
No, sir.

44:15.694 --> 44:16.779
Throw it some prey.

44:16.862 --> 44:19.156
We're out of test subjects, sir.

44:21.283 --> 44:22.534
We still have one left.

44:34.672 --> 44:36.840
Hey. Come out.

44:45.349 --> 44:46.266
Hey!

44:47.267 --> 44:48.102
Hey!

44:49.937 --> 44:50.938
Help me out.

46:04.178 --> 46:05.596
Yukiko Maeda?

46:06.221 --> 46:07.097
Dear me.

46:08.974 --> 46:11.018
You already know who I am,

46:12.561 --> 46:14.396
Ms. Yoon Chae-ok.

46:23.363 --> 46:24.448
This is strange.

46:24.948 --> 46:29.036
The Japanese officers
have suddenly quieted down.

46:38.337 --> 46:40.547
Papers! Get your papers.

46:41.131 --> 46:42.841
Papers!

46:44.635 --> 46:45.886
Get your papers!

46:46.470 --> 46:47.471
Papers!

46:48.639 --> 46:50.057
And the Jongno Police Station?

46:50.140 --> 46:54.520
They don't seem to have found
the whereabouts of Yoon Chae-ok either.

46:57.064 --> 47:00.400
Then why have they gone so quiet?

47:01.193 --> 47:05.113
Normally, they would have turned
Bonjeong and Jongno upside down by now.

47:05.197 --> 47:08.408
Whatever it is, I find it quite different
from how it used to be.

47:09.159 --> 47:11.453
They're also keeping quiet
about Ichiro's death.

47:14.623 --> 47:15.457
Master.

47:15.541 --> 47:17.125
Mrs. Nawol. How did it go?

47:17.626 --> 47:18.877
It went well.

47:25.175 --> 47:29.221
But I think you need to head downstairs.

47:29.304 --> 47:30.973
You have a visitor.

48:01.003 --> 48:02.004
Well then,

48:03.088 --> 48:04.256
I'll leave you two alone.

48:24.526 --> 48:25.527
What brings her here?

48:25.611 --> 48:26.695
I'm not sure.

48:28.280 --> 48:30.782
They're just sitting there
without much to say.

48:31.658 --> 48:36.538
Wait, I don't see Beom-o.
Where could he have gone?

48:37.289 --> 48:38.123
Forget about him.

48:39.875 --> 48:41.293
He's not coming back.

48:51.261 --> 48:53.096
That woman, Mrs. Nawol,

48:54.556 --> 48:55.974
is she trustworthy?

48:58.226 --> 49:00.604
She's been like family
since I was a child.

49:02.105 --> 49:05.400
Just because they're like family
doesn't mean you can trust them.

49:06.568 --> 49:10.697
You shouldn't trust people so easily.

49:12.157 --> 49:14.368
They don't betray you
because they are evil.

49:14.451 --> 49:17.329
They betray you because they are weak.

49:18.914 --> 49:22.584
And most human beings are weak.

49:29.132 --> 49:30.968
What is the reason for this visit?

49:31.051 --> 49:34.096
So, don't bother waiting.

49:36.181 --> 49:39.726
Ms. Yoon Chae-ok will not be coming back.

49:42.479 --> 49:43.313
What do you mean?

49:43.397 --> 49:44.648
I just told you.

49:45.482 --> 49:48.694
Betrayal is caused not by evil,
but by weakness.

49:51.571 --> 49:53.782
That woman wasn't strong enough

49:55.033 --> 49:56.410
to stay by your side.

49:57.411 --> 49:58.745
Do you know where she is?

50:00.664 --> 50:01.999
Where is she?

50:03.917 --> 50:05.460
Lady Maeda!

50:06.503 --> 50:07.337
She is dead.

50:11.550 --> 50:12.801
And guess what.

50:12.884 --> 50:18.265
I liked you much better
before you went to Ongseong Hospital.

50:19.099 --> 50:22.436
You clearly differentiated
what would bring you profit versus loss.

50:23.103 --> 50:24.187
Simple-minded.

50:25.605 --> 50:26.857
Hence, powerful.

50:30.694 --> 50:31.528
Please

50:32.571 --> 50:34.239
return to your former self.

50:35.615 --> 50:38.660
Forget about Ishikawa, Akiko,
and Ongseong Hospital.

50:39.828 --> 50:41.246
Even Yoon Chae-ok.

50:42.372 --> 50:43.832
Forget all about that woman.

50:45.375 --> 50:47.252
Just live your life like before,

50:48.378 --> 50:50.881
as if nothing had ever happened.

50:52.799 --> 50:56.136
Do that, and you
and the House of Golden Treasure

50:57.763 --> 50:59.056
will be safe.

51:03.268 --> 51:04.853
Be careful, Mr. Jang!

51:04.936 --> 51:06.480
There is an invisible hand

51:08.273 --> 51:09.775
that controls everything.

51:12.986 --> 51:14.154
How did you find out?

51:17.032 --> 51:18.617
I pulled every string

51:19.576 --> 51:23.497
in Bonjeong and Jongno,
but couldn't even find a trace of her,

51:23.580 --> 51:24.581
so how…

51:26.708 --> 51:30.212
how is it that you know about her death?

51:33.173 --> 51:34.674
If it wasn't for me,

51:36.093 --> 51:38.095
you would have been arrested already.

51:39.513 --> 51:43.058
The fact that you were close
with the woman who shot Director Ichiro

51:44.226 --> 51:47.062
is enough to classify you as seditious.

51:48.271 --> 51:49.314
So,

51:50.440 --> 51:52.776
don't do anything dangerous anymore,

51:53.610 --> 51:54.444
Mr. Jang.

51:54.528 --> 51:56.363
Where is Yoon Chae-ok?

51:56.446 --> 51:58.907
I told you. She is dead.

51:58.990 --> 52:00.826
Then let me see her body.

52:00.909 --> 52:02.035
Stop…

52:04.037 --> 52:05.705
disappointing me.

52:07.874 --> 52:09.709
I don't want us to become enemies.

52:09.793 --> 52:11.002
Yoon Chae-ok!

52:13.505 --> 52:14.673
Where is she?

52:18.426 --> 52:22.097
You will never see her again.

52:54.546 --> 52:57.841
I don't care what you've done.
I will find her.

52:58.633 --> 53:02.971
Whether she's dead or not,
I will find her, no matter what!

53:08.685 --> 53:11.813
Are you saying you plan to go against me?

53:11.897 --> 53:15.400
How can someone like me
possibly be a match for you?

53:16.818 --> 53:20.405
You're a Japanese citizen with power
from a mighty family--

53:20.488 --> 53:22.073
If you know that, stay quiet.

53:23.491 --> 53:25.160
You'll be safe that way.

53:25.243 --> 53:26.328
Even so!

53:29.122 --> 53:30.373
This is about Yoon Chae-ok.

53:32.375 --> 53:34.878
I may run a petty pawnshop,

53:35.378 --> 53:37.631
I may have lived a life without pride

53:37.714 --> 53:41.343
doing all sorts of crap so I could get by,
but for once in my life,

53:42.260 --> 53:45.597
I wanted to protect her,
even if I had to give up all that I have.

53:45.680 --> 53:46.848
So?

53:48.892 --> 53:51.102
Just how will you go against me?

53:51.811 --> 53:52.979
With what?

53:54.898 --> 54:00.237
Not those pieces of trash
by your side, I hope.

54:00.320 --> 54:03.323
Watch your mouth. They are my people!

54:03.406 --> 54:08.078
Do you even know
how those people betrayed you?

54:08.745 --> 54:11.623
That woman, Mrs. Nawol,
whom you consider family.

54:12.415 --> 54:15.001
She ratted out your mother
a long time ago.

54:16.336 --> 54:19.756
My mother is in there too.

54:19.839 --> 54:21.591
Have you seen her?

54:22.092 --> 54:25.262
Her name is Sim Sun-deok.

54:27.639 --> 54:29.224
Do you know her?

54:30.016 --> 54:30.850
No.

54:30.934 --> 54:33.103
You haven't heard her name either?

54:34.354 --> 54:35.438
I haven't.

54:45.115 --> 54:48.201
SIM SUN-DEOK

54:58.044 --> 54:59.462
That man, Gu Gap-pyeong,

55:00.338 --> 55:03.675
recently betrayed you
in the police bureau's torture chamber.

55:03.758 --> 55:06.177
I will…

55:10.265 --> 55:12.267
tell you everything now.

55:13.560 --> 55:14.561
Everything…

55:19.482 --> 55:20.734
And that kid, Beom-o?

55:21.234 --> 55:24.487
To find his mother who left him
and ran away to Japan when he was a kid,

55:25.322 --> 55:26.698
he betrayed you.

55:27.449 --> 55:29.868
He sold you out
for a cheap passage ticket,

55:30.577 --> 55:33.580
even when you've treated him like family.

55:34.956 --> 55:36.958
And your so-called friend?

55:37.834 --> 55:42.380
It took him only a few hours to confess
that you and your friends were key rebels.

55:44.132 --> 55:48.636
That's what humans do
when they are pathetically weak.

55:50.013 --> 55:53.975
So desperate to save their own skin
that they forget the favors they received.

55:54.059 --> 55:55.602
They have no morals.

55:56.936 --> 55:57.937
And yet,

55:58.897 --> 56:01.524
what did you say you'd do
with those pieces of trash?

56:03.068 --> 56:04.402
You'd go against me?

56:06.154 --> 56:09.741
When I'm the one working tirelessly
for you, even at this very moment?

56:11.409 --> 56:13.036
You say you'll betray me?

56:14.371 --> 56:16.998
Is that what you're saying, Mr. Jang?

56:28.885 --> 56:29.803
Fine.

56:32.055 --> 56:33.640
You may be right.

56:36.726 --> 56:37.644
But

56:38.812 --> 56:39.813
did you know?

56:41.731 --> 56:43.149
None of those people

56:44.984 --> 56:46.945
would have gone through those things

56:48.196 --> 56:49.781
had the world been different.

56:53.576 --> 56:55.203
If the world had been different,

56:56.996 --> 56:58.748
they wouldn't have ended up in jail

56:58.832 --> 57:02.335
and beaten to near death
so as to betray their friends.

57:03.086 --> 57:07.382
They wouldn't have gotten burned
or had their nails plucked out.

57:07.465 --> 57:12.137
And they wouldn't have had to give in,
give up the names of their friends,

57:13.221 --> 57:15.723
and live the rest of their lives
wracked with guilt.

57:16.641 --> 57:18.393
But despite all that,

57:19.352 --> 57:22.105
they're fighting tooth and nail
and living with the pain

57:24.023 --> 57:27.819
because they need to survive,
no matter how humiliating and shameful!

57:29.946 --> 57:31.364
We have to survive,

57:32.615 --> 57:35.493
or no one will remember
what we went through.

57:39.372 --> 57:41.875
So don't you dare
call them pieces of trash.

57:44.335 --> 57:45.545
Not a single one of them

57:47.714 --> 57:51.301
deserves to be called such
by the likes of you.

58:04.772 --> 58:05.773
So…

58:07.901 --> 58:08.943
that's your choice.

58:11.321 --> 58:12.322
Exactly.

58:15.158 --> 58:16.201
This is my choice.

58:19.829 --> 58:21.122
This is it for us.

58:23.458 --> 58:24.667
Lady Maeda.

58:51.778 --> 58:52.779
Let's go inside.

58:54.781 --> 58:55.698
The night

58:57.367 --> 58:58.451
is still cold.

59:31.818 --> 59:32.777
Master!

59:34.237 --> 59:35.154
Master!

59:35.989 --> 59:36.990
Master.

59:39.075 --> 59:40.076
What did I…

59:42.912 --> 59:44.914
What did I just say out there?

59:48.167 --> 59:49.377
You were being yourself.

59:52.088 --> 59:54.090
You said everything there is to be said.

59:56.050 --> 59:57.093
Just wait.

59:59.929 --> 01:00:01.514
I will find the clues…

01:00:04.434 --> 01:00:06.102
to Yoon Chae-ok's whereabouts…

01:00:09.606 --> 01:00:12.150
before I die.

01:00:24.120 --> 01:00:25.163
Tae-sang.

01:00:28.291 --> 01:00:29.709
When did you find out?

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:32.962
That I…

01:00:35.840 --> 01:00:37.133
gave up…

01:00:40.178 --> 01:00:41.471
your mother's name?

01:00:43.765 --> 01:00:44.724
It was…

01:00:49.854 --> 01:00:52.065
a little after Mother passed away.

01:00:57.070 --> 01:00:57.987
And you…

01:01:00.740 --> 01:01:01.658
still

01:01:02.909 --> 01:01:04.494
took me in?

01:01:09.666 --> 01:01:12.335
Because I didn't think it was your fault.

01:01:26.683 --> 01:01:28.017
Don't worry too much.

01:01:31.187 --> 01:01:32.480
You know Mr. Gu.

01:01:33.314 --> 01:01:35.316
Once he sets his mind on something,

01:01:37.110 --> 01:01:39.362
he always comes back with a hint.

01:01:42.073 --> 01:01:43.157
Let's wait.

01:01:47.120 --> 01:01:48.621
What if it's true?

01:01:53.584 --> 01:01:54.961
What if she really is dead?

01:02:22.029 --> 01:02:23.197
Is the prey ready?

01:02:23.281 --> 01:02:25.783
Lady Maeda sent us a Josenjing woman.
